 "model": "2x2 effective propagator; exact for two interacting branches. Uses only eigenvalue differences, so it is invariant under rescaling of the spectral condition (residue-based excitation factors are not).",
 "question": "No EP survived verification, so: how close does the ringdown come to EP phenomenology anyway?",
 "answer": "Not close. The strongest interactions split almost entirely in Im omega (damping) rather than Re omega (frequency): the two branches do not coalesce, one simply decays faster. The EP template beats a single damped exponential by only ~2.4x while using twice as many free amplitudes, which is not evidence of secular growth. A large t_beat/tau here reflects near-equal oscillation frequencies, NOT an approach to an EP.",
